WEBVTT

00:00:12.340 --> 00:00:16.180
O Lord, please save my father.

00:00:22.430 --> 00:00:25.060
That was a superb performance,

00:00:25.060 --> 00:00:26.650
my queen.

00:00:32.360 --> 00:00:37.490
Edward had everything that I never could.

00:00:37.490 --> 00:00:41.200
He was the spitting image
of our father and a perfect man.

00:00:41.200 --> 00:00:42.750
But...

00:00:42.750 --> 00:00:44.290
You look dreadful.

00:00:47.750 --> 00:00:51.090
Richard...

00:00:52.670 --> 00:00:56.010
You're no longer a king.

00:00:56.010 --> 00:00:58.640
It's time to die, Brother.

00:01:00.760 --> 00:01:03.480
Your time has come, Edward.

00:01:05.520 --> 00:01:12.780
Let us go to atone for the sins that not
even a royal fortune could spare you.

00:01:16.990 --> 00:01:18.280
As you say,

00:01:19.410 --> 00:01:20.530
Warwick.

00:01:26.620 --> 00:01:28.710
York of the white rose.

00:01:28.710 --> 00:01:31.250
Lancaster of the red rose.

00:01:31.250 --> 00:01:37.760
These royal houses with roses for
their crests battled for the throne.

00:01:37.760 --> 00:01:42.470
People call their strife
the "Wars of the Roses."

00:03:17.320 --> 00:03:22.240
In the name of the Father, the Son,
and the Holy Ghost. Amen.

00:03:42.510 --> 00:03:44.470
That was certainly abrupt.

00:03:44.470 --> 00:03:49.850
Death takes irresistibly
and without warning.

00:03:49.850 --> 00:03:53.020
Just like killing on the battlefield.

00:03:53.020 --> 00:03:54.730
Death must be busy.

00:03:57.610 --> 00:04:03.200
Buckingham, do you remember
the first person you killed?

00:04:03.200 --> 00:04:06.120
No. What of it?

00:04:06.120 --> 00:04:09.120
I just recalled mine.

00:04:09.120 --> 00:04:11.290
John Grey,

00:04:11.290 --> 00:04:13.250
Elizabeth's former husband.

00:04:14.250 --> 00:04:18.130
I'd heard he was slain
by some nameless soldier.

00:04:18.130 --> 00:04:20.840
Why tell me this?

00:04:20.840 --> 00:04:22.970
I swore to keep no secrets.

00:04:29.390 --> 00:04:32.140
I wagered all I have on you.

00:04:32.140 --> 00:04:34.140
Don't betray me.

00:04:38.190 --> 00:04:41.030
Today is All Fool's Day!

00:04:41.030 --> 00:04:43.900
Men are women, and children are adults!

00:04:43.900 --> 00:04:48.160
In this world gone mad,
a beggar can even become a king!

00:04:48.160 --> 00:04:50.370
Would you like a crown of your own?

00:04:51.660 --> 00:04:55.120
I could never be king.

00:04:55.120 --> 00:04:59.630
Why not? This is a world gone mad.

00:04:59.630 --> 00:05:02.710
Even a demon could be king here.

00:05:02.710 --> 00:05:07.010
Your Grace, I bring urgent
tidings from Lord Hastings.

00:05:07.010 --> 00:05:09.760
Earl Rivers means to
make himself Protector.

00:05:09.760 --> 00:05:14.520
He is escorting the Prince of Wales
to the palace with a large army.

00:05:14.520 --> 00:05:17.100
I have troops in readiness as well.

00:05:17.100 --> 00:05:19.770
I'll leave to meet the prince at once.

00:05:19.770 --> 00:05:23.820
By escorting the new king and
making a show of our dignity

00:05:23.820 --> 00:05:28.660
I, Anthony Woodville, Earl Rivers,
shall secure my place as Protector.

00:05:28.660 --> 00:05:33.700
Fetching the prince isn't your only job.

00:05:33.700 --> 00:05:37.370
You're to seize Richard
and bring him to the Tower.

00:05:37.370 --> 00:05:41.920
He murdered John.
I mean to execute him personally.

00:05:43.840 --> 00:05:48.760
Thank you for telling me
the truth about John's death.

00:05:48.760 --> 00:05:53.770
Buckingham, my kingmaker.

00:05:53.770 --> 00:05:56.180
Once he learns of Earl Rivers's actions,

00:05:56.180 --> 00:06:00.060
he's certain to give chase
at the head of a large army.

00:06:00.060 --> 00:06:05.030
You're to call on him alone
and dine amicably with him.

00:06:05.030 --> 00:06:08.320
Once he's off his guard,
arrest him for treason.

00:06:08.320 --> 00:06:11.740
But what if his troops surround me?

00:06:11.740 --> 00:06:17.580
In that event, the troops
I have in readiness

00:06:17.580 --> 00:06:19.500
will kill Richard.

00:06:21.540 --> 00:06:24.000
Ugh! What are these clothes?!

00:06:24.000 --> 00:06:26.420
I don't want to go to the palace in these!

00:06:26.420 --> 00:06:27.550
Your Royal Highness--

00:06:27.550 --> 00:06:28.680
Call me "Majesty"!

00:06:28.680 --> 00:06:30.720
I am your king!

00:06:30.720 --> 00:06:33.430
M-My apologies, Your Majesty.

00:06:33.430 --> 00:06:35.390
Spoiled little shit.

00:06:35.390 --> 00:06:37.560
And I lack for companions.

00:06:37.560 --> 00:06:40.060
Why hasn't Richard joined us?

00:06:40.060 --> 00:06:44.730
He's close at hand.
Earl Rivers has gone to fetch him.

00:06:44.730 --> 00:06:49.070
Please, Your Majesty,
take your ease here tonight.

00:06:53.200 --> 00:06:56.080
Welcome, Richard!
I've been waiting for you!

00:06:56.080 --> 00:06:59.540
Earl Rivers. Is this your whole party?

00:06:59.540 --> 00:07:01.330
It is. What of it?

00:07:01.330 --> 00:07:06.300
He's supposed to have an army.
What's the meaning of this?

00:07:06.300 --> 00:07:08.550
Where is the Prince of Wales?

00:07:08.550 --> 00:07:12.760
Pardon my saying so, but you
appear too few for his guard.

00:07:12.760 --> 00:07:16.060
Now, let us rest from our travels!

00:07:16.060 --> 00:07:18.980
I was certain that you would come!

00:07:18.980 --> 00:07:24.190
I take it you've brought
these forces to defend us?

00:07:24.190 --> 00:07:27.110
Oh, my dear brother-in-law!

00:07:27.110 --> 00:07:29.440
For the sake of His Late Majesty's repose,

00:07:29.440 --> 00:07:33.280
let us join hands in support
of our new sovereign!

00:07:33.280 --> 00:07:34.990
Have some wine.

00:07:34.990 --> 00:07:38.290
We shall both enjoy ourselves this night!

00:07:42.370 --> 00:07:47.300
The earl seems to have drunk too much.
Bear him to his chambers.

00:07:47.300 --> 00:07:49.050
I'll retire as well.

00:07:50.260 --> 00:07:54.090
It appears your master's
fears were unfounded.

00:07:54.090 --> 00:07:57.640
I hope so, but I'm not so sure.

00:07:59.100 --> 00:08:02.730
"Join hands in support
of our new sovereign"?

00:08:02.730 --> 00:08:05.900
I desire stability for
the Royal Family of York.

00:08:05.900 --> 00:08:09.110
I even sacrificed George to secure it.

00:08:10.150 --> 00:08:15.200
That day, why did my father
decide to become king?

00:08:15.200 --> 00:08:19.450
A light that I can wish
for but never obtain.

00:08:22.000 --> 00:08:23.710
Who goes there?!

00:08:23.710 --> 00:08:24.710
A thief?

00:08:28.460 --> 00:08:30.590
I suggest you keep quiet.

00:08:30.590 --> 00:08:35.430
If the truth about your body gets out,
you'll burn at the stake.

00:08:35.430 --> 00:08:37.430
Who are you?

00:08:37.430 --> 00:08:41.890
Forgotten, have you?
I remember you clear as day.

00:08:43.600 --> 00:08:46.060
In an abandoned shack in the woods

00:08:46.060 --> 00:08:49.980
was a child in a dirty cloak
and ill-fitting chain mail.

00:08:49.980 --> 00:08:52.360
And beneath it lay...

00:08:53.650 --> 00:08:55.780
...a demon's body.

00:08:55.780 --> 00:08:58.280
It can't be! You were there?

00:08:58.280 --> 00:09:02.200
You must think your soldiers
will keep you safe.

00:09:02.200 --> 00:09:06.120
Well, I've got an army on my side too.

00:09:06.120 --> 00:09:07.580
Isn't that right,

00:09:07.580 --> 00:09:09.750
Your Grace, the Duke of Buckingham?

00:09:09.750 --> 00:09:11.960
Buckingham?!

00:09:11.960 --> 00:09:15.680
Won't you deny this man's ravings?

00:09:17.180 --> 00:09:19.100
What are you after?!

00:09:21.470 --> 00:09:22.600
Do it.

00:09:27.480 --> 00:09:30.190
Look. This proves he's a demon.

00:09:37.160 --> 00:09:40.700
I wasn't convinced until
I saw with my own eyes.

00:09:40.700 --> 00:09:42.410
Now do you get it?

00:09:42.410 --> 00:09:47.710
He's a demon, sent into the royal
family to bring England to ruin!

00:09:47.710 --> 00:09:50.960
It's strange. I feel nothing.

00:09:50.960 --> 00:09:53.050
This is a natural outcome.

00:09:53.050 --> 00:09:54.550
Light

00:09:54.550 --> 00:09:57.300
will never shine on a demon.

00:09:58.390 --> 00:10:01.760
I knew God was watching over me.

00:10:01.760 --> 00:10:06.020
Now, where's the title and gold
you promised me, Your Grace?!

00:10:06.020 --> 00:10:08.350
I'll grant your wish.

00:10:13.690 --> 00:10:15.240
What is this about?

00:10:15.240 --> 00:10:20.280
Any further conversation would
lower the value of my soul.

00:10:20.280 --> 00:10:23.830
Are you going to execute me?

00:10:23.830 --> 00:10:28.370
Earl Rivers will arrest you
for treason at dawn.

00:10:28.370 --> 00:10:32.710
The Woodvilles have no intention
of sharing power with you.

00:10:32.710 --> 00:10:37.720
And with this body,
you're hardly "worthy" of the crown.

00:10:37.720 --> 00:10:38.880
I see.

00:10:40.510 --> 00:10:42.890
Why did you hide it from me?

00:10:42.890 --> 00:10:46.640
Did you think the knowledge
would make me despair?

00:10:46.640 --> 00:10:50.190
Did you fear to lose me?

00:10:50.190 --> 00:10:51.440
You?

00:10:51.440 --> 00:10:55.820
Yes. When we first met,
I took you for a woman.

00:10:55.820 --> 00:10:57.400
And my imagination was correct.

00:10:57.400 --> 00:10:58.860
Stop! I'm--

00:10:58.860 --> 00:11:02.700
A man? True, you are that.

00:11:02.700 --> 00:11:05.870
But has your "womanhood" ever known love?

00:11:05.870 --> 00:11:09.870
You've always lived with
your true self hidden.

00:11:09.870 --> 00:11:11.750
I can tell.

00:11:11.750 --> 00:11:13.380
We're two of a kind.

00:11:15.630 --> 00:11:22.510
If you offer your hidden self to me,
I'll be the partner of a demon.

00:11:22.510 --> 00:11:23.640
Demon.

00:11:23.640 --> 00:11:24.600
Demon.

00:11:24.600 --> 00:11:26.140
Bloodstained demon...

00:11:26.140 --> 00:11:27.350
Who defied...

00:11:27.350 --> 00:11:29.180
...the will of God.

00:11:29.180 --> 00:11:31.850
Richard, this is your last chance.

00:11:31.850 --> 00:11:37.610
Will you seize your desire,
or perish empty-handed?

00:11:38.940 --> 00:11:40.070
Come.

00:11:41.990 --> 00:11:45.530
Say it. What do you truly want?

00:11:45.530 --> 00:11:49.750
Admit that you want
what you've always desired!

00:11:51.290 --> 00:11:52.920
I want...

00:11:54.830 --> 00:11:57.090
What do you want?

00:11:57.090 --> 00:11:58.760
I want...

00:11:58.760 --> 00:12:01.470
I want the crown!

00:12:02.680 --> 00:12:05.890
I'll give you the crown.

00:12:07.560 --> 00:12:10.350
Remember this pain.

00:12:10.350 --> 00:12:13.560
It's the seal of our pact.

00:12:13.560 --> 00:12:16.190
The pain of our mutual sin.

00:12:17.940 --> 00:12:23.530
I prayed and wished, but the voices
of my curse never faded.

00:12:23.530 --> 00:12:29.790
If the lost warmth I've foolishly
clung to can never be mine again,

00:12:29.790 --> 00:12:32.910
if it will allow me to escape destiny...

00:12:35.000 --> 00:12:37.790
I'll become a demon.

00:12:47.390 --> 00:12:48.890
Are you awake?

00:12:50.850 --> 00:12:53.560
I've had fresh clothes prepared for you.

00:12:53.560 --> 00:12:55.440
I'll help you dress.

00:12:56.770 --> 00:13:00.650
The Woodvilles believe
that I've betrayed you.

00:13:00.650 --> 00:13:01.860
Your Grace.

00:13:02.690 --> 00:13:07.740
Don't worry. Last night,

00:13:07.740 --> 00:13:10.080
I carried Richard to bed.

00:13:11.620 --> 00:13:17.380
Now, Rivers must be dreaming
of himself on the throne about now.

00:13:22.300 --> 00:13:25.430
Good morning, Earl Rivers.

00:13:25.430 --> 00:13:29.600
Goodness. I drank too much
last night to put him off his guard.

00:13:29.600 --> 00:13:31.720
Now, is all as we planned?

00:13:31.720 --> 00:13:32.720
Naturally.

00:13:34.060 --> 00:13:37.520
This will make me the
mightiest man in England!

00:13:37.520 --> 00:13:39.980
I'll be kinglier than the king!

00:13:41.230 --> 00:13:45.450
Anthony Woodville, Earl Rivers,
commands you in the king's name!

00:13:45.450 --> 00:13:47.860
Seize the traitor!

00:13:48.950 --> 00:13:51.450
Wh-What are you doing?!
Don't arrest <i>me</i>! Seize--

00:13:51.450 --> 00:13:53.160
Earl Rivers.

00:13:53.160 --> 00:13:55.290
R-Richard!

00:13:55.290 --> 00:13:56.830
Stop! Damn it all!

00:13:56.830 --> 00:13:58.710
You betrayed me, Buckingham!

00:13:58.710 --> 00:14:01.630
I've merely seen justice done.

00:14:01.630 --> 00:14:04.260
<i>You </i>are the traitor.

00:14:04.260 --> 00:14:05.420
Rivers.

00:14:11.430 --> 00:14:13.770
Unhand me! What's this about?!

00:14:13.770 --> 00:14:15.100
My mother will make you pay!

00:14:15.100 --> 00:14:18.350
--Imprison the rebels in my castle.
--I said, unhand me! Let go!

00:14:18.350 --> 00:14:20.060
--Buckingham,
--Don't you know who I am?!

00:14:20.060 --> 00:14:22.730
--we're going to collect
His Royal Highness.
--Take your filthy hands off me!

00:14:24.650 --> 00:14:26.150
The prince is here!

00:14:26.150 --> 00:14:30.120
It's Prince Edward--I mean, King Edward V!

00:14:30.120 --> 00:14:31.320
God save the king!

00:14:31.320 --> 00:14:33.740
God save His Royal Majesty!

00:14:33.740 --> 00:14:35.160
God save the king!

00:14:37.040 --> 00:14:38.330
At last...

00:14:38.330 --> 00:14:40.830
At last, the time has come!

00:14:40.830 --> 00:14:45.420
My blood--Woodville blood--
will rule over the blood of York.

00:14:45.420 --> 00:14:50.510
John, I'll bless and avenge your death.

00:14:50.510 --> 00:14:55.930
Richard the sinner! You will paint
this festival red with your blood

00:14:55.930 --> 00:14:59.190
without so much as setting
foot in London again.

00:15:00.150 --> 00:15:04.730
Your Majesty, and my beloved younger bro--

00:15:04.730 --> 00:15:05.860
Mother!

00:15:11.110 --> 00:15:14.160
I have just returned,

00:15:14.160 --> 00:15:16.200
my dear sister-in-law.

00:15:16.200 --> 00:15:17.790
Mother!

00:15:21.420 --> 00:15:23.380
Richard.

00:15:23.380 --> 00:15:26.340
Where are my brother and Grey?

00:15:26.340 --> 00:15:30.720
Queen Elizabeth, I bear
regrettable tidings on that subject.

00:15:30.720 --> 00:15:33.720
I wanted to hurry on to London,

00:15:33.720 --> 00:15:36.430
but Rivers and Grey went
and got themselves arrested!

00:15:36.430 --> 00:15:38.060
Wh-What?

00:15:38.060 --> 00:15:44.980
They spoke honeyed words and
concealed venom in their hearts.

00:15:44.980 --> 00:15:48.610
They schemed to charge me
with crimes I did not commit.

00:15:48.610 --> 00:15:50.240
Impossible! Nonsense!

00:15:50.240 --> 00:15:52.660
He's the one who plotted rebellion!

00:15:52.660 --> 00:15:55.200
Guards! Seize Gloucester!

00:15:56.700 --> 00:15:58.620
Curse you useless lot!

00:15:58.620 --> 00:16:01.790
Dorset has taken leave of his
senses! Defend His Majesty!

00:16:01.790 --> 00:16:04.080
What?! Damn you!

00:16:04.080 --> 00:16:05.880
Wait! Don't let him escape!

00:16:05.880 --> 00:16:07.800
Dorset.

00:16:07.800 --> 00:16:12.050
I don't believe it.
He abandoned his mother and fled.

00:16:12.050 --> 00:16:15.390
You are safe now, Your Majesty.

00:16:15.390 --> 00:16:21.100
I shall purge England of all villains
who would disturb its peace.

00:16:21.100 --> 00:16:22.980
Let us proceed to the palace.

00:16:25.150 --> 00:16:27.650
What could have happened?

00:16:27.650 --> 00:16:29.320
This...

00:16:29.320 --> 00:16:30.940
This can't be...

00:16:33.360 --> 00:16:37.160
The palace is now free of your enemies.

00:16:37.160 --> 00:16:41.830
Does Elizabeth still trust you?

00:16:41.830 --> 00:16:45.380
I have many ways to ensure that she does.

00:16:45.380 --> 00:16:48.500
She's even called me her "kingmaker."

00:16:49.710 --> 00:16:52.090
What, are you jealous?

00:16:52.090 --> 00:16:55.840
You're <i>my </i>kingmaker.

00:16:55.840 --> 00:17:00.850
Elizabeth still has her uses.
Pretend to be her ally.

00:17:00.850 --> 00:17:03.730
Of course, my king.

00:17:03.730 --> 00:17:05.020
Your Grace.

00:17:05.020 --> 00:17:07.440
His Majesty summons you.

00:17:07.440 --> 00:17:08.520
Very well.

00:17:14.320 --> 00:17:19.080
Spying is a fine hobby. I'll let you
watch to the end next time.

00:17:19.080 --> 00:17:25.250
I told you that I'll show no mercy
to anyone who harms His Grace.

00:17:25.250 --> 00:17:30.750
But if he wishes it,
even if it will harm him...

00:17:30.750 --> 00:17:36.630
I've become a demon's partner
to grant Richard's wishes.

00:17:36.630 --> 00:17:38.550
Can you do as much?

00:17:38.550 --> 00:17:41.510
Can you stain your hands with God's blood?

00:17:44.140 --> 00:17:46.980
He discovered the whole plot,

00:17:46.980 --> 00:17:49.360
including your involvement.

00:17:50.480 --> 00:17:54.900
Don't you mean that
you revealed it to him?

00:17:54.900 --> 00:17:58.910
Or have you been in league
with him all along?

00:17:58.910 --> 00:18:01.660
Never. I have proof.

00:18:01.660 --> 00:18:04.370
Or should I say... a witness?

00:18:06.540 --> 00:18:07.670
Mother.

00:18:07.670 --> 00:18:08.580
Beth?!

00:18:09.830 --> 00:18:13.840
I asked Buckingham to help Richard.

00:18:13.840 --> 00:18:15.340
What?!

00:18:15.340 --> 00:18:19.390
I can never face him with
a smile again because of you!

00:18:19.390 --> 00:18:22.890
Uncle Anthony and Grey
only got their just deserts!

00:18:22.890 --> 00:18:28.270
You should be grateful that
Buckingham still forgave you!

00:18:28.270 --> 00:18:31.900
Consider a wise daughter
your greatest treasure.

00:18:31.900 --> 00:18:37.070
I suggest you give up open involvement
in government and seek sanctuary.

00:18:37.070 --> 00:18:40.950
That will spare Richard a
dreadful decision as well.

00:18:43.030 --> 00:18:46.710
I see I have no choice.

00:18:46.710 --> 00:18:48.000
Very well.

00:18:50.380 --> 00:18:53.800
In exchange, I'll take the
younger prince with me.

00:18:53.800 --> 00:18:57.590
If you deny me,
I'll take my life this instant.

00:18:57.590 --> 00:19:00.300
You don't want me to die yet, do you?

00:19:01.850 --> 00:19:03.470
As you wish,

00:19:04.890 --> 00:19:06.890
Your Majesty.

00:19:09.480 --> 00:19:12.310
Thank you for inviting me tonight.

00:19:12.310 --> 00:19:14.650
Our enemies are no more!

00:19:14.650 --> 00:19:16.940
Yes. To our king.

00:19:16.940 --> 00:19:18.030
To the king.

00:19:21.610 --> 00:19:24.330
My wine hasn't tasted
so fine in many a night.

00:19:24.330 --> 00:19:29.370
All thanks to your timely
warning, Lord Hastings.

00:19:29.370 --> 00:19:34.340
Think nothing of it!
We've long been comrades in arms!

00:19:34.340 --> 00:19:36.590
But we can't relax yet.

00:19:36.590 --> 00:19:39.340
Not while that woman is the queen mother.

00:19:41.220 --> 00:19:43.680
Then let's send someone to watch her.

00:19:43.680 --> 00:19:46.720
I know just the woman: Jane!

00:19:46.720 --> 00:19:48.890
Your witch?

00:19:48.890 --> 00:19:50.940
Well, mine at the moment.

00:19:50.940 --> 00:19:55.320
Intercourse with a witch seems
to bring superhuman pleasures.

00:19:55.320 --> 00:19:57.570
Enough to make you putty in her hands.

00:19:57.570 --> 00:20:03.070
Oh, no, the bond between us
is one of simple love.

00:20:03.070 --> 00:20:07.200
Although I admit that its beginning
was quite stimulating.

00:20:07.200 --> 00:20:12.580
I thought so. To open a tight-closed
bud, begin with a shock.

00:20:15.170 --> 00:20:18.090
We can depend on Hastings's support.

00:20:18.090 --> 00:20:21.720
No. He supports Edward.

00:20:23.930 --> 00:20:25.850
Why are you upset?

00:20:25.850 --> 00:20:27.890
Why did you look at me that way?

00:20:27.890 --> 00:20:30.770
That way? What way?

00:20:30.770 --> 00:20:33.100
Don't tell me you thought that

00:20:33.100 --> 00:20:37.230
one time would be sufficient
to purchase my soul.

00:20:37.230 --> 00:20:38.730
I'll undress myself.

00:20:41.490 --> 00:20:45.410
Lord Richard?
Is something wrong with your left eye?

00:20:45.410 --> 00:20:49.830
The servants' children
called my eyes strange.

00:20:49.830 --> 00:20:52.620
Even Mother always says so.

00:20:52.620 --> 00:20:55.960
Why am I different?

00:20:55.960 --> 00:20:58.960
It isn't love that I want.

00:20:58.960 --> 00:21:02.090
I need a pact.

00:21:02.090 --> 00:21:06.800
Now, grave more pain into me
to your heart's content.

00:21:06.800 --> 00:21:09.600
Before the wound of our pact heals.

00:21:09.600 --> 00:21:14.140
My skin color is different.
Is that strange?

00:21:14.140 --> 00:21:16.560
No, not at all.

00:21:16.560 --> 00:21:20.610
You're not strange either, Lord Richard.

00:21:20.610 --> 00:21:23.320
You still don't understand.

00:21:23.320 --> 00:21:26.410
Mere pain fades quickly.

00:21:26.410 --> 00:21:28.160
I told you:

00:21:28.160 --> 00:21:31.120
Offer your secret self to me.

00:21:31.120 --> 00:21:35.710
Listen, Richard. I'm about to mark you...

00:21:35.710 --> 00:21:38.080
I'll hide it with my hair.

00:21:38.080 --> 00:21:41.800
If you hide it, you won't feel sadness.

00:21:43.590 --> 00:21:46.090
...with sweet suffering.

00:21:48.300 --> 00:21:50.390
Can you do as much?

00:21:50.390 --> 00:21:52.470
What can I do?

00:21:52.470 --> 00:21:55.270
Yes. This is fine.

00:21:55.270 --> 00:22:00.940
Richard, only I know the true you.

00:22:00.940 --> 00:22:03.860
Even pleasure becomes pain.

00:22:03.860 --> 00:22:07.360
In this ceremony that
resembles love, I will be killed

00:22:07.360 --> 00:22:08.870
and reborn.

00:22:13.240 --> 00:22:15.580
Listen well, all of you.

00:22:15.580 --> 00:22:18.540
The weak, mad King Henry VI

00:22:18.540 --> 00:22:22.840
could not rule England
without his uncle's help.

00:22:22.840 --> 00:22:26.590
I'm no incompetent, but this is tradition.

00:22:26.590 --> 00:22:33.260
Yes. That man required
a Protector even in adulthood.

00:22:33.260 --> 00:22:35.180
The situation is different.

00:22:35.180 --> 00:22:37.600
Now, my lords, I trust that we are agreed?

00:22:37.600 --> 00:22:40.650
What choice is there with Rivers gone?

00:22:40.650 --> 00:22:44.320
No one who objects would
be here in the palace.

00:22:44.320 --> 00:22:49.610
Richard, Duke of Gloucester,
we name you our Lord Protector.

00:22:49.610 --> 00:22:52.030
I humbly accept.

00:22:57.830 --> 00:23:02.000
The light that my father
almost seized back then.

00:23:02.000 --> 00:23:05.050
This is a transient light.

00:23:05.050 --> 00:23:11.430
Back then, we were but powerless
children dreaming of the future.

00:23:11.430 --> 00:23:15.430
A crowd stood between us and the crown.

00:23:17.100 --> 00:23:21.440
But now there are only
two princes in our way.

00:23:21.440 --> 00:23:24.230
Now, seize the rose!

00:23:24.230 --> 00:23:25.610
Even if

00:23:25.610 --> 00:23:28.780
my hands end up drenched in blood.
